- [x] Edit mode: Being able to ctrl+right-click drag to form an area (web has some unoptimized implementation of this), all the sands inside that rectangle formed will be selected. I can then group/ungroup them (as options of controls next to sand).

- [x] Build the Information tab. It has version (cargo), port, and directory of Lince. In that same tab also have:
	- [x] Add to Information panel info on commit downloaded version of Lince, last updated info, updates available button to download and restart Lince (if possible, according to OS, i understand that NixOS might not work, it's ok, show message if it cant).
	- [x] The Bevy interface (native.rs) has no update UI yet. That's the one thing waiting on the frontend/backend channel you're building (crates/cell). When it lands: call utils::self_update::net::run_watch_loop with AssetKind::Desktop, automatic = <setting>, and render on_available as a panel notice + Download-and-restart action. Everything it needs is already in utils. Staying current. Lince keeps itself up to date from its own published builds — one shared checker in the backend; server mode and the Box both use it. It checks the release feed about once a day and verifies the update list against Lince's signing key before trusting it; a list that fails is refused. In server mode, when updates are allowed, it downloads the new build, verifies its checksum, replaces the running program and restarts — it never asks. In the Box the same finding is a quiet notice in the Information panel: the new version and a button to download and restart; when updates are automatic it applies the same way without asking. The Box notice should arrive through the frontend/backend channel once that exists; until then the Box runs its own copy of the checker. When Lince cannot replace its own file — system package manager, or the Nix store — it says so and gives the one command instead. The running version and commit show in the panel, and a build with no version stamp is marked so it is clear why an update cannot be compared. People receive notification when can update, and clicking it brings them to information tab with update related ui and interactions.

