- [ ] Castles should be separated from sand in the picker. Basic blocks and packaged workflows. One can select a protein and change the way it's data is shown from a sand to a castle, castle to castle... If i change the way i present the protein and it is missing a field, i can choose to only show the properties that appear in the original or fill the remaining ones. If i have more properties than the new castle shows, it can discard it or add to the final piece.

- [ ] We have castles (group of sands, locked, one bundle of data coming from protein, with every bundle showing as the same castle we made). It would be good to be able to maintain a group, meaning we still maintain the sands as being generated in a certain way, filling certain sands per bundle, but one sand of the group is unlocked, meaning it is not glued to the group. I will move the glued sands of the group and it will not follow along necessairily. It is detatched. If i end up changing the protein and not showing a certain "row" of data, the bundle/group will be gone, the locked and unlocked parts of that "row", it is still part of the group, just unlocked. I can unlock all of the group or just one sand.

- [ ] Have a way to edit one sand based on it's uid or the uid of one record it has a property of, not all the sands that spawn from the protein of that record. So if i want to edit a circle i made, or the sand of my record Apple it feels like im just editing singular stuff that will be persisted if we have an update on protein that serves the Apple record.

- [ ] Be able to copy a sand from the group, duplicating the showing of one property in two sands (should be normal behavior, it's not 1 on 1 data-sand) and detatching it from the group, so it maintains the original sands, plus an unlocked that is a copy of a sand of the castle, still belonging to the group, but unlocked.
- [ ] When editing we should have a way to edit a part of the sand, just it's visuals of the sand, just the links, the protein, the visual and links... no need to bombard them with all of the information at once.
- [ ] When composing sands, we might choose to give it it's normal size as the minimal one, if we give a maximum it will have some respective form of scroll of the content inside if it occupies it all. If we dont give it a max it will grow, so we can have either our full documents or a scrollable version of them.
	- [ ] The focus can be a way to take a sand with a maximum and showing it with no limit, in the center of the screen, it is different from editing a sand to have no limit, the focus is like entering the data being shown. It's like the current Record sand, that shows everything. But this would be showing all the contents of one sand, no scroll or anything, maybe centered and occupying a big portion of the screen, a focus, really.
		- [ ] We can also take a property and show a focused view of the Record it belongs to. Similar to today's html Record sand.

- [ ] The temporal part of the needs is central to Lince. The interface should find a smart way to deal with it. We can start with a simple calendar sand, that is a castle sand made of some buttons and one special made calendar one that can take time related properties of records and show as first class citizens of it, because it is a native calendar/timeline sand, not an area of influence for time properties. In the future we might want to discover a way to turn it into lower primitives, but a ready made calendar sand is ok too.

- [ ] What if we could put shaders in the sand? We have wgpu, shouldnt be too hard to slap a custom WGSL into the surface of the sand, maybe even making the sand be the actual body and the wgsl going out of it, if it glowed it could show as a light outside of the sand. If we are using compute/vertex shaders in the interface, putting something custom to make it pretty should be fairly straightforward to the users.

- [ ] Using Simulation to see the how things would change if we performed some action, or some rule where enacted, or some transfer completed could all be simulation related visualizations.

- [ ] The Record editor’s five-second return from source to rendered text (anicca/interface/ official-sands.md:178) would go. I’d keep the current block stable until the person leaves it or deliberately changes presentation. Thinking for five seconds should not cause the editor to transform beneath the caret.
- [ ] Explain which forces, sorting rules, pins and immunity affect a Sand. Provide limits and pause controls when rules conflict or keep triggering one another.

- [ ] Explore if there is a way to use some pandoc equivalent in bevy so we can have document showing out of the box.
	- [ ] In any way, we should have mostly compliant with markdown syntax for record descriptions and provide Raw, Pretty and Pragmatic views of Markdown, with slash commands, images, checkboxes and Record references. Keep the current source block stable until the person leaves it or deliberately changes presentation. Also would be good to write mermaid, typst is cool too.

- [ ] Connect to an Organ, sign in, reconnect and sign out from the native interface. Show which Person and Organ are active, and keep work intended for that Organ there.
- [ ] Create vocabulary, saved Protein views and workspaces from an empty Organ. Let people arrange their own work without requiring a company template or a project for every Record.
- [ ] Make Record, Table, Todo and Kanban work together: search, create, edit, assign, filter, sort and act on several Records. Show which changes succeeded and which were refused.
- [ ] Build the Access Control Castle with Actors, Roles and Permissions. Let an administrator choose which Records and properties each Role can read or change, preview the result, recover access and revoke it from already-open clients.
- [ ] Show activity and Trash, with ways to restore permitted Records and recover useful drafts. Give administrators the server's health, backup and recovery information.

## Box and saving

- [ ] Drop a supported file or URL onto Box and choose a suitable Sand. Explain unavailable formats; displaying something must not silently create a Record.
- [ ] Keep interface state in memory and save it to a readable file at a configurable frequency. Show unsaved changes and the last saved state; recover from an interrupted save.
- [ ] Undo and redo complete gestures, including group, connection and appearance changes. Save reusable composition separately from personal camera, focus and selection.
- [ ] Let other programs and Fiote inspect and arrange Box through the same checked operations. Their changes must be attributed, visible and undoable.
## Showing Protein data

A Protein area uses one group as a template and fills it once for each result. For example, each task might become a title, an assignee and a quantity. Showing the same property twice creates two views of the same data.

- [ ] Choose a Protein, see the fields it returns and connect them to Sands in a result template. Keep room for labels, buttons and decoration that have no data binding.
- [ ] Keep each result's appearance stable through edits, reordering and refresh. When a result disappears, remove its appearances and keep their settings for the stated recovery period.
- [ ] Explain why a Sand is here: its source, field, group, local changes and layout. Show empty, loading, withheld and broken data as different states, with ways to repair a connection.
- [ ] Change the presentation of a Protein between Sands and Castles. Preview matching, missing and extra fields, including affected local edits, and let the person cancel or undo the change. Hiding a field only changes its presentation.

## Editing one appearance

Editing Apple's title Sand should feel like editing that one thing. Pear and another appearance of Apple should keep their own settings. The Record uid can help find appearances; the person chooses which one to edit.

- [ ] Edit one loose Sand or one child of a Protein result, and keep that change after refresh and restart.
- [ ] Release one or all children from moving with a group while keeping their data and ownership. Reattach them without a jump. If the result disappears, its released children disappear too.
- [ ] Copy and release a property Sand so both copies show the same data. A click or edit must still cause only one intended Action.

## Organ, contacts and devices

People should be able to see and control the sharing that already happens behind the interface.

- [ ] Show every contact and what they can see of this Organ in one place, with a link to change each contact's settings.
- [ ] Give each device separate controls for what it can see and what it can do. Let the owner narrow a device's access while keeping it connected.
- [ ] Show the identity succession chain so changes of Organ identity can be understood.
- [ ] Choose direct or mailbox delivery per contact. Explain delivery limits and reconnect when a contact's device list is missing.
- [ ] Move a Record to another Organ through an offer the recipient can accept, with progress and cancellation controls.
- [ ] Put invitations, replica grants, Record moves and Transfer invitations in one pending-offers list. Show the local outcome clearly while respecting any rule that keeps refusal private from the sender.
- [ ] Show when Lince last checked its stored view against its log, what it found and what needs attention. An unchecked state must not look healthy.

## Grouping, Calendar and Clock

Start with arrangements that stay still. Assignee and due date can organize tasks along two directions while those properties also remain visible on the cards.

- [ ] Turn displayed properties into grouping and sorting Areas. Preview the arrangement, handle missing and multiple values, and let a manually moved Sand return to following the layout.
- [ ] Build Calendar with agenda, day, week and timeline views over Record dates. Show points, intervals, all-day work, unscheduled work and overlapping entries.
- [ ] Use Karma's occurrences for repeated work, with timezone and date editing support. Distinguish changing one occurrence from changing its series, and provide keyboard alternatives to dragging.
- [ ] Build the Clock over the same entries: the next hour from above, and a spiral with a chosen future horizon in perspective. Show intervals, repetitions and overdue work; holding the view's time must not stop Karma.

## More workflows

The remaining workflows reuse the same controls, editor, Protein and Actions. Each needs a usable interface and any missing backend operation together.
- [ ] Complete Ontology and Relations for exploring Concepts, directed Assertions, Trails and progress. Moving the graph's layout must not change its relationships.
- [ ] Bring Transfer inspection and lifecycle controls into native Sands, showing participants, quantities, direction, permissions and delivery outcomes.
- [ ] Build Karma's Program, Frequency, candidate and grant controls. Show cycles and other refusals beside their cause, and distinguish a proposed effect from one that actually ran.
- [ ] Complete contact and conversation workflows, then calls and media with their own backend support. Keep ordinary discussion usable independently of calls or Fiote.
- [ ] Make Instinct readable and let a person deliberately import its tutorial Records. Explain when tutorial content is unavailable.
- [ ] Complete Archive and Sand Publisher for inspecting, validating, importing, exporting and publishing the selected content. Show scope, package identity and notices before acting.
- [ ] Share published Sand packages between connected Organs without requiring a central registry. Preserve their author, identity, origin, permissions and licenses even when a recipient cannot run them yet.
- [ ] Let the AI composition surface show a proposal for review and apply it through ordinary authorized operations. Explain unavailable providers and unapplied changes.

## Sharing a workspace

Sharing Records and sharing a Box layout are different choices. Protein's Synchronization area should make both understandable alongside File Sync.

- [ ] Invite viewers and editors into a live workspace, with one hosting Cell saving the agreed changes. Give each person their own camera and selection, with optional shared presence.
- [ ] Show pending changes, refusals, reconnect progress and access loss. If the host is unavailable, explain what the saved read-only view contains. Offline editing and replacing the host need a separate design.
- [ ] Keep workspace editing permission separate from permission to read or change the Records shown inside it.

## Movement and spatial views

After ordinary editing is comfortable, Areas can make Box move. Avian handles contact physics; Lince decides which data an Area affects and what entering it means.

- [ ] Build the Kanban Castle from configured Areas, including the Concept and quantity choices already listed in the Record. Keep a direct, stationary arrangement available.
- [ ] Shape terrain with raise, lower, flatten and smooth tools. Allow effects fixed in the workspace or attached to a Sand, and show which Records each effect applies to.
- [ ] Switch between top and perspective views of the same surface. Add free 3D placement with a previewable, undoable conversion back to a flat workspace.
- [ ] Keep a Sand facing its authored direction by default, with a Face viewer option. Changing the camera or reading face must not change its physical behavior.
- [ ] Choose whether Protein results appear directly, travel from a spawn point or settle before appearing, and how quickly they arrive. Save useful settled positions without writing every animation frame.
- [ ] Let Laboratory run headlessly to check motion and replay problems. Keep off-camera behavior consistent and state the limits of repeatability.

## Effects and simulation

Visual effects change appearance. Simulation previews possible changes to Lince data. Both should remain understandable and easy to leave.

- [ ] Add shader presets and a supported WGSL editor for Sand surfaces, including bounded outward glow. Keep text readable, preserve the last working effect and provide Reset and Disable outside the customized content.
- [ ] Preview an Action, Karma Rule or Transfer beside the current state. Show assumptions, affected Records, dates and unknown consequences without making real changes.
- [ ] Apply an accepted proposal through ordinary Actions after checking that its source data is still current. Calendar and Clock should work before these previews are available.

## Specialized content

Some old Sands relied on a browser inside Lince. Each needs a suitable native implementation or an explicit external opening option before returning.

- [ ] Add native document reading, terminal, video, game and animation support as needed. Keep the surrounding controls in Bevy and include each embedded dependency's notices.
- [ ] Bind a terminal to a task Record, open it from that Record and change the binding without killing the shell. Keep the person's interactive shell separate from an agent's read-only command output.
- [ ] Explore the website wish in Lince.lingua without assuming CEF. Any proposed embedded view must explain how it isolates storage and permissions from Box; the current no-browser direction and this wish still need a workable answer.

## Checking the result

Each feature is finished when a person can use it through the real controls and backend. An entry in the picker, an old checkmark or a test fixture alone does not establish that.

- [ ] Check editing, navigation and recovery with keyboard, pointer, text composition and a screen reader. Review light, dark and custom themes, reduced motion and the available display scales.
- [ ] Check collaboration with two people, including rejected edits, live access revocation, reconnect, restart and backup recovery. Preserve locked content and author-private drafts.
- [ ] Keep an idle workspace quiet and one active Sand from updating every static one. Measure responsiveness and memory on the owner's machine, including large workspaces and repeated opening and closing.
- [ ] Walk through the real controls before suggesting tutorial text for the owner to add to Lince.lingua.

One useful walkthrough is Apple and Pear from the same Protein: customize only Apple, copy and release its quantity, move the remaining group, remove and restore the result, change Castle with a missing field, focus and edit, then restart. Check that the intended appearance, data and unfinished work survive each step. Repeat the important operations with keyboard and assistive technology.

Fiote's session controls, tool timeline, model settings, budgets and agent orchestration belong with Fiote in Lince.lingua. The shared conversation and terminal requirements above stay here. [The remaining Fiote interface details](sands.md) are kept as prose for that section's manual review. Shallow collaborative-text snapshots are a backend storage improvement, also separate from interface completion.

# Complete v1.0.0 (may have things pushed to part A):

These remain possibilities for the owner to consider, without an implementation order: offline editable workspace copies and host replacement; portals between stacked workspaces; richer Protein filters; formulas; drawing inside Record bodies; previewing the Records and Assertions that a description would create; maps and world scenes; production, stock, logistics and ordering views; and public commerce. [Future ideas](../deferred.md) and [world and production notes](../future-sands.md) retain their meaning.

